Initial public release: MATHESIS Continuous Geometric Computing Language v1.0

- mathesis_isa.h: ISA definition (opcodes 0x01-0x09, Stiefel manifold S^{D-1})
- mathesis_compiler.py: .mth source -> 64-byte aligned binary compiler
- mathesis_studio.html: browser IDE with real Float64Array(2048) execution
- facturacion_geometrica.mth: billing system in pure MATHESIS (7 instructions)
- test_lyapunov_dreaming.mth: LYAPUNOV_DREAM opcode demo, drift=2.22e-16
- MANUAL_MATHESIS_SABIOS_ARIEL.md/.docx: full bilingual manual
- README.md: project overview (EN/ES)

MATHESIS is a continuous-geometry computing language operating natively
on the Stiefel manifold S^{D-1} (D>=2048). Zero 1D token serialization
between AI reasoning steps. Compatible with COCONUT and LatentMAS research.

Silicon verified: Exit Code 0, AMD A4-6300, 2026-11-07
